{%- comment -%}
  Store row — owned by sections/main-stores.liquid.

  One stockist in the locator list: retailer eyebrow → branch name → optional
  address. A <button> so it's keyboard-operable; clicking flies the map to this
  store's pin (handled by assets/store-map.js).

  Expects:
    - store (metaobject) with field handles: retailer, location
      (coordinates + optional store_code live on the metaobject too but aren't
       rendered here — store_code is internal, coordinates feed the map JSON in
       the section)
    - index (integer) — forloop.index0 from the section, must match the store's
      position in the section's JSON coordinate blob so row ↔ pin line up

  See CLAUDE.md → "Snippet Ownership". The `stores` metaobject does not exist in
  the live store yet — see the section comment for the field handles to create.
{%- endcomment -%}

<li class="store-row" role="listitem">
  <button class="store-row-button" type="button" data-store-row data-store-index="{{ index }}">
    {%- if store.retailer != blank -%}
      <span class="text-h1 store-row-retailer">{{ store.retailer }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if store.location != blank -%}
      <span class="text-h3 store-row-name">{{ store.location }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </button>
</li>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Hairline between rows, mirroring .news-index-grid: symmetric block padding
     with a top border on every row but the first puts the hairline centred in
     the gap. */
  .store-row {
    display: block;
  }

  .store-row:not(:first-child) {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .store-row-button {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxs);
    width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--spacing-s) var(--spacing-xs);
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .store-row-button:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-input-bg-hover);
  }

  /* Active = this row's pin is focused on the map (class set by store-map.js
     on the button, which carries the [data-store-row] hook). */
  .store-row-button.is-active {
    background-color: var(--color-accent-light);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
